<%= skill %>

Review the changes between `<%= base_ref %>` and `<%= head_ref %>` in this
repository. The changed files are:
<%- files.each do |file| -%>
- <%= file %>
<%- end -%>
<%- if diff_path -%>

The unified diff of these changes is in `<%= diff_path %>`; read it with the
Read tool rather than running git. The working tree is at `<%= head_ref %>`.
<%- end -%>

Run the review as the skill describes, then report every finding that
survived your own verification as structured output. Do not post comments,
push, or modify files.

For each finding:
- `file` is the repo-relative path exactly as listed above.
- `affected_lines` use new-side line numbers at `<%= head_ref %>`; only report
  lines added or modified in the diff.
- `tags` include the review pass that raised the finding as `pass:<name>`
  (for example `pass:security`, `pass:edge-cases`), plus any topical tags.
- `severity` and `confidence` use these integer scales (1 is most severe /
  most confident):

Issue severity scale:
<%= severity_scale %>

Confidence scale:
<%= confidence_scale %>

<%= show_threshold_text %>
<%= severity_rubric %>
If you are unsure whether a finding clears the "shown at all" bar above, lean
toward NOT reporting it. If nothing qualifies, return an empty `issues` list.
<%- if inline_json -%>

Your final reply must be only this JSON object, with no prose around it:
{
  "issues": [
    {
      "file": "<repo-relative path>",
      "title": "<issue_title>",
      "details": "<issue_description>",
      "tags": ["pass:<name>", "<tag>", ...],
      "severity": <1-4>,
      "confidence": <1-4>,
      "affected_lines": [{ "start_line": <int>, "end_line": <int or null>, "proposal": "<code or null>" }]
    }
  ]
}
<%- end -%>
